NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1058,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,2,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":2.9387,"rank":0.0523,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV001201","role":"target","render":{"description":"Predictions that a sick man will recover, will plough first with a white horse and later with a black horse, and that the black horse will pull the hearse, come true. The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43204","original":"Voorloop. \nSchoenmaker vertelt.\n\nOal Kamies noast ons was de haile winter al aon 't sukkeln.\n't Gung dan veur-, dan achteroet,\nBuurman Wessels was 't er op 'n dag hèn west te kieken, hou d' oale 't muik.\n\"Kamies gait achteroet, hai hoal 't nich meer,\" zee hai.\nMoar opa, oal Steffen, zee.\n\"Nee Wessels, Kamies wordt weer beter.\nHai hef nou 'n wit peerd. En 't volgend veurjoar plougt hai 't land mit 'n zwaarde. \nDat zwaarde peerd brengt hum vot.\" \n't Widde wör verkoft en 'n zwaarde kwam d'r veur in de ploats.\nEen buurman hef hiermit de grond pluigd.\nVolgende zömmer störf Kamies.\nVeur de woagen zol 'n peerd van de buren.\nKamies zien aigen har er nog nooit veur west en doarum wol ze hom laiver nich broeken. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV000905","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Before there is a road, the sound of a dog cart and the barking of dogs is heard.","place":"Ter Apel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43087","original":"Maar wel is het waar, dat veel mensen in het veen een hondekar hebben horen ratelen. Ook hoorden ze de hond blaffen.\nLang voor er een weg was en voor er later inderdaad een hondekar langs trok.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.87667,7.05972]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006906","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that one day many soldiers would come with wagons without horses. When the Canadians arrive in 1945, someone remembers this.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43580","original":"Veurloop.\nt Is n hail zet leden. Oabram zee es n moal: “Hier koomt nog ais n haile bult seldoatn. Ik zai ze bie t hoes van H. en bie K en op t haim van Z. Zai hebt woagens bie zuk zunder peerden.\n Toun in 1945 de Canadezen kwamen, was dr nog aine oale, dei zuk dat vertelsel van de spoukkieker in t zin schoot. Hai lag op berre en kun nait best wat zegn, omdat e verlamd was. \nMoar zoveul begreepn wie wel van zien “hoi, hoi”, dat e zegn wol:“Oabram zee t ja al?”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV008709","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Noise in the horse stable in the evening is an omen that a horse will kick something to pieces.","place":"Wessinghuizen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45305","original":"t Gebeurde wol is, dat ze s oavends wat in t peerdstaal heurden. Kiekn deden ze maistied nich, man ze wuzzen wol, dat t peerd gauw wat stukn hou-en zol; door was t n veurbeduudsel van.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.0525,7.075]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessinghuizen.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2327,"rank":0.4579,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053808","role":"member","render":{"description":"When magpies chatter in the garden by the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25423","original":"As eksters op 'e tún by hûs skatterje, dan komt der in sterfgefal.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ064413","role":"member","render":{"description":"Chattering magpies around the house mean that there will soon be a death in that house.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27273","original":"As der eksters om 't hûs hinne skatteren, dat bitsjutte ek, dat der yn dat hûs mei gauwens ien stjerre soe.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"EGGEN004809","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Appearance of a werewolf, someone wearing a sheepskin.","place":"Itteren","prov":"L.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208097","original":"- over de weerwolf:\n\nde weerwouf haet hei auch gezete. dat waor eine mèt 'n sjaopsvèl um. bie 't geulhòut ('n planken bruggetje over de geul) mòt 'r höbbe gezete.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ026610","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the old days people were afraid when magpies came to the door, because that meant a death.","place":"Boelenslaan","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21410","original":"As der eksters by de doar kommen wienen de minsken froeger bang. Hwant dat bitsjutte in deade.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Itteren belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1129,"rank":0.1883,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ045306","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A dog with four eyes is a ghost-howler. When the dog begins to howl ghostly, it is usually an omen of an impending death.","place":"Ureterp","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24269","original":"Ik hie in houn mei fjouwer egen. Dat binne spoekgûlers. Sy ha twa ljochte flekken boven de egen.\nUs buorjonkje krige in sinnestek. Dy jouns om sa'n tsien ûre hinne bigoun ús houn hiel jammerlik to gûlen. Us oare buorman sei: \"Hjir gebeurt fannacht hwat.\" Dy nachts is it buorjonkje stoarn.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV012201","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A man sees things in advance: someone will one day own four horses, a funeral going to a churchyard that is laid out later, the colour of the horse before the hearse, wagons without horses.","place":"Wessinghuizen","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43723","original":"Was es n keer n zekere Vos achter de Holte, dai veuroet zain kön; spuik kiekn nuimen ze dat. \nWur voak over hum verteld, man ain ding muik ik zulm mit. \nIk stön n moal op de dele; ik keek noar de peern en dou kwam d oale dr aan. \n\"Kiek\", zee hai, \"ie hebt doar vaier peern bie de krubbe stoan en dat heb ik vieftig joar leden al zain.\"\n Mien boerderij stön dr dou nog nich en toch zag dai olle Vos dat er vaier peern bie de bak stönnen te hoaver vreetn.\n\nZo zag dai olle ook begravvenisn. \nDoar kwammen wol es wonderlieke dingen bie veur, dai hai nich verkloarn kön, man dai loater toch oetkwammen. \nZo zag hai n liekstoatie deur t dörp goan, man nich noar t kerkhof tou. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ013030","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Four young men once heard the sound of carpentry while nothing could be seen. Not long afterwards there were builders' huts there.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19490","original":"Doe't ik nog jong wie roan ik us mei Diuwe Jelle en Durk - en Willem Mozes de Sânwei del yn 'e Harkema, dat nou de betonwei is, de Wytfeanster kant út. Doe hearden wy alle fjouwer klear dat se dêr oan 't houtendakspikerjen wienen. It timmere dêr hiel ûngelyk.\nMar dêr stie neat, gjin kerl, noait ien spier, fordomd.\nEven letter stienen dêr de boufakhuzen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"4052a6c321df4088","accepted_hashes":["2010f712af7abe5198479d1fc7106184e703848880c970a1514bbd1bf555fa6a","646d4e9ec014ca0406475c75253a8788ccaef7c6690c2687c7ff7ab1431ddc7b","9825971eb99496325b16779c73ac97bf1855ee7166e51368e5461afe4f48c230","a6e1f4d19117c380cc8584aaf3bf6c55d3b267099459b60f7b88fb2464479454","c1654b2719a68b2789bb7838b2aa45dd827a1ef737430bf196e2f0c552bb007f","c8d69a84d72080aaba3ba8f1171efa38f6fe4110f32ea436337cd73a8445bb2a"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2226,"rank":0.7299,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"member","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST279","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmhand brings the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Tilligte","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"B.R.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13623","original":"Door ouden wordt nog van de Wit Wieve verteld, die alleen kwaadaardig waren, wanneer ze getergd werden. Zo wordt verteld dat een boerenknecht eens het spit bracht naar de plaats, waar zij woonden. Hij werd door eene der witte wieve achtervolgd, doch hem niet kon inhalen, omdat ze in de haast maar een schoen had kunnen aantrekken. Toen de knecht het huis binnenvluchtte, wierp ze hem met een bijl achterna, die in de steil (deurpost) terecht kwam.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEUNING005102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A white ghost that floats over a gate into the field at night turns out to be a sheep.","place":"Drachten","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131150","original":"Sa ha se it yn Jistrum ek hast hâwn. Der laei njonken de hurde wei in brede mei gêrs bigroeide berm. En dêr kamen de stikken lân mei hikken op 'e daem op út. Nachts seach min hiel faek in wyt ding oer in hikke it lân yn sweven. Fansels, dat wie gjin goed spul. Fêst tsjoenderij. Mar hjir kaem ek ien, dy net oan sok spul leauwde en dy 't útmakke, dat it in drint (heideskiep) wie, dat fêst it gêrs yn de berm lekkerder foun as dat yn it lân.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"member","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Drachten belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0539,"rank":0.5763,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BIJLSMA007506","role":"card","render":{"description":"Sighting of a woman dressed in white with a veil, travelling in a spinning butter tub.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130656","original":"Alde Houwing fan Sumar wie in \"wedergeboren man\". Houwing wie op in moaije simmermoarn oan de marswâl to melken mei in faem en in jonge. Hja seagen op it wetter hwat oankommen. It wie to lyts foar in boatsje, it like wol in bûteraed. Dêr siet it boppe-ein fan in frommiske yn, by de mul omt-ôf alhiel yn it wyt, mei in wale oer de holle. It boatsje bigoun as in top to draeijen. Houwing en de beide oaren wienen op it lân delfallen. Doe 't hja wer seagen, wie it skynsel fuort. It barde by Sumar mids de 19 de ieu.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0296","role":"card","render":{"description":"White ladies haunted 't Slot. Many people did not dare to go near it because of them.","place":"Tienhoven","prov":"Utr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50997","original":"Bij 't Slot* spookte 't altijd. D'r liepen dames in het wit. Een hoop mensen, die d'r niet heen dorsten.\n\n*Ameide","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ035001","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a white lady on a horse used to be seen often. She is a ghost woman.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22709","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei by de Harkema ried froeger in wite dame op in hynder, doe wie de Lytse Wei noch in sânpaed.\nDurk Pitstra hat har us njonken him hawn op in joun, doe siet er op syn eigen hynder om dat yn 't lân to bringen. Hwat hurder hy ried, hwat hurder dat frommes tasette. Hy koe har net kwyt wurde en dreau op 't lêst yn 't swit.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ031811","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two witte wieven (white women) always stroll about a haunted spot. At the same place a funeral procession once got stuck: the wagon ended up in the ditch, coffin and all.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22060","original":"It Langpaed rint fan Readskuorre nei de Surhuzumer tsjerke. Dêr kuijeren altyd twa wite wiven. Dy spoeken dêr.\nFroeger woarden de minsken warskôge: \"Tink der om, gean dêr net lâns.\"\nDêr mat us in bigraffenis lâns kom wêze. De wein mei kiste en alles is doe yn 'e sleat rekke.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093907","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three witte wijven (white women) used to haunt the Lange Laan. People did not dare to pass there at night.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34614","original":"Op 'e Lange Loane spoeken froeger trije wite wiven.\nForskate lju doarsten by nacht de loane net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Goutum. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Goutum"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c5","word":"two","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.6858,"rank":0.6322,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"top","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","half":"top"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0094","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A dog appears and she throws a handkerchief in front of it. Back home she sees remnants of the handkerchief between the boy's teeth, so he must be a werewolf. The planned marriage is called off when it turns out that the boy has a secret power to bring harm to people and because he is a werewolf.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1183","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Then a few people put their heads together and agreed to teach that man a lesson. They went there with a gun, and on the bullet they had put a split dime. That man was lucky he was not out walking that evening.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0804"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"GENDT026","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"This happens by putting on a wolfskin hidden somewhere. Then he goes out to frighten people, or he jumps on their back and becomes very heavy. He makes them carry him as far as the houses or until it gets light.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0801"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"LYST236","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"While the unfortunate man is playing cards, everyone stays seated until it strikes twelve. The bewitched man grows more and more nervous, but everyone simply stays put. On the stroke of twelve the werewolf's skin rolls in down the chimney and is burnt in the fireplace amid loud cheering. The man is released from the spell.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"VODA_002_12","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They call in a priest to free the farmhand from his enchantment. The priest does this by burning the werewolf's skin.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0095","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When he comes back the boy reassures the frightened girl and nothing more happens. At home, however, the girl sees bits of her apron between his teeth, and she breaks off the courtship.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"LYST178","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The girl walks on and meets a werewolf. She throws away her handkerchief and flees. The werewolf tears the handkerchief apart. A little later she meets the boy again. There are still bits of her handkerchief between his teeth. She broke off the engagement.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"VODA_041_11","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"as it is often depicted elsewhere, but someone who jumped on lonely travellers at night and had himself carried on their backs.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0801"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0549","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Then they heard a kind of roaring. They also said that the sheep had been torn apart by the werewolf.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0803"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"GENDT030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He sees the werewolf at the agreed spot, strikes the axe through the bread and then against the werewolf's arm. The werewolf turns back into a human and is freed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0822"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ052012","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"As a werewolf, her husband regularly has to bite into something. Red yarn shows in his molars. Werewolves especially like to sink their teeth into red wool.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0824. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c4"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c4"],"stack":["c1","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0698,"rank":0.4838,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0294","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"General fear of the white lady.","place":"Ameide","prov":"Utr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50995","original":"DE WITTE JUFFROUW\n\nBij 't Slot had je de witte juffrouw. Veel mensen waren d'r bang van. Maar m'n vader, dat was vroeger een stroper, ok van de armoei....werken van donker tot donker....en dan 's-avonds weer op stropen uit....maar die was niet bang van de witte juffrouw!","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ090105","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. One of seven sisters is a nightmare. A nightmare enters the house through the keyhole.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33428","original":"Fan sawn jonges is ien in wjerwolf.\nFan sawn famkes is ien in nachtmerje.\nIn nachtmerje komt troch 't kaeisgat yn 'e hûs.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ019728","role":"member","render":{"description":"Of seven brothers, one is often a werewolf, usually the eldest or the youngest. Such a werewolf has the nature of a wild animal.","place":"Sweagerbosk","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20528","original":"Fan 'e sawn bruorren is faek ien in wjerwolf. It is de âldste of de jongste. Hjir wie sa'n húshâlding. Dat wie Lammert Roek. De jongste, seinen se, wie in wjerwolf. Sa'n wjerwolf hie de natuer fan in wyld dier.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ041909","role":"member","render":{"description":"The eldest or the youngest of seven successive daughters is a nightmare. With seven sons, it is a werewolf.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23774","original":"Fan ien fan 'e sawn dochters, dy't op elkoar folgje, sûnder jonges der tusken is de âldste of de jongste in nachtmerje. Fan ien fan 'e sawn soannen is ien in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Ameide belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0054,"rank":0.2821,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST189","role":"door","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELS001721","role":"card","render":{"description":"Man has to walk around with a werewolf for two days.","place":"Grashoek","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210547","original":"Weerwolven:\nIk heb eens horen vertellen van een man in Kessel, die twee dagen met een weerwolf op zijn rug moest lopen. Hij werd hem eindelijk kwijt, door hem tussen twee dicht bijeen staande bomen af te wringen. Hij had de klauwsporen op zijn borst staan.\n\nVerslag 50, Omzetting van de verhalen, verteld door Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden, doorgegeven onder no. L291-17, op 26-12-1962. Van Nederl. versie in plaatselijk dialect. Helden, 4 nov. 1969\nIch heb èns huuëre vertèlle van enne mins in Kèèssel, dè twieë daag mèt te wèèrwolf hei motten drage. Hè woord öm kwiet, dor öm tössen twieë buim, die kort bei-ein sjtonge, van de rök te vringe. Later hei ’n de klauwsjpóre nag op zien boorst staon.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.3521,"rank":0.9612,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011305","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"Once when a man was out in the field, a very small brown dog floated past him. It headed for the canal. The man asked what the dog wanted, but the little creature disappeared into the water. Exactly three weeks later the same thing happened to the man's father. Then too the dog seemed to disappear into the canal. The place was uncanny.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17744","original":"Us Hindrik-om fortelde, dat syn heite broer hie us op it fjild west yn Houtigehage. Doe hie dêr in hiel lyts brún hountsje by him lâns sweefd. 't Gong op 'e feart yn.\n\"Hwat mastû, lytse kleine?\" hied er sein. Mar it hountsje wie samar fuort west, krekt as wie 't yn 'e feart wei woarn.\nKrekt trije wiken letter kom syn heit presys itselde oer. Doe like it hountsje ek yn 'e feart weiwoarn to wêzen. It hie ek by syn heit lâns sweefd. It hat forkeard spul west.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"Voda_022_02","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"A sexton accidentally locks an old woman who is praying in the church. At 12 midnight she woke with a start. All the candles lit up. The ghost of a dead priest asks whether anyone can help him with the mass. The woman does not answer out of fear. A boy is bolder and helps the priest. In his lifetime the priest had read a mass in a state of sin. Now his soul is released.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":null,"initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129733","original":"Ik heb dus hier een verhaal, dat ik in België heb mogen noteren, van eene priester die zelf een fout begaan had in zijn leven. En toen na zijn dood als een geest terug moest keren om te proberen die fout te herstellen. Het verhaal is mij verteld in het Belgische dorpje Baarle, en luidt als volgt. Daar in het dorpje Baarle, daar woonde vroeger een zeer vrome vrouw. En die zat op zekere avond in de kerk verzonken in gebed. En ze was zo verdiept in het gebed dat zij niet hoorde hoe de koster de sleutel in een sleutelgat stak om de kerkdeur te sluiten. En omdat de koster haar ook niet had opgemerkt, werd ze in de kerk opgesloten en was ze genoodzaakt daar de hele nacht door te brengen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEMP251","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"A bold maidservant who sees a ghost at night pulls its shirt off, thinking it is a joke. Back home she finds out it is a real shroud of a deceased relative of her master. A clergyman tells her she must put the shirt back on the ghost, or she will find no rest. She succeeds, but after what she went through, she did not live three more days.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43100","original":"Het doden- of geestenhemd\n\nIn een herenhuis op het Sint-Servatiusklooster, achter de Sint-Janskerk te Maastricht, woonde eens een dienstmeisje dat voor niets bang was.\nOp zekere dag kwam iemand haar vertellen dat er achter Sint-Jan alle nachten tussen twaalf en één een spook liep, dat maar alleen een hemd aanhad.\n'Daar ben ik niet bang voor!' zei het meisje, 'als het komt, trek ik het zijn hemd uit!'\nEn 's nachts ging zij achter Sint-Jan, op het spookuur, de geest afwachten. Nauwelijks had het dan ook twaalf uur geslagen, of daar vertoonde zich het spook, juist zoals men het haar had verteld. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ002518","role":"inside","render":{"description":"A newly married man goes to an inn in Kromelle for a drink. He stays a long time and has to go home in the dark. A little dog follows him past the firewood, down the paths that run diagonally across the fields. The little dog is a warning, and it makes sure the man never goes to the inn again.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/15624","original":"Heit hâldde wol fan in slokje. Yn 't bigjin fan 't trouwen kocht er ien yn Kromelle. Dear bleau er nochal even sitten. Doe soed er de jouns nei hûs ta. Mar doe kom him in hountsje \nefterop en dat wie net by him wei to slaen. It folge him almar. It paed gong oer de houtsjes, de skeanpaden del.\nIt hountsje is ûnderweis net wer by him weigong. It folge him op 'e hielen, oan hûs ta. It wie in pleachbist en foar heit in warskôging. Hy hat noait wer yn 'e herberch west.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 3.","3 — 12 — 3."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"4052a6c321df4088","accepted_hashes":["442497926eb775d00fe035c048e2efa52b11f0fccf09b3b0a90310025c737d6f"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.567,"rank":1.3,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053402","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happens that a dead person cannot find rest because a promise made to him was not kept. If the minister addresses the dead about his unfulfilled wish and that wish is then fulfilled, the dead finds rest. If something still has to be handed to the dead, you must roll it up in a handkerchief and hold the corner of the handkerchief. If you do not do it this way, your skin will be scorched off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25362","original":"It gebeurt soms wol us, dat ien dy't to hôf brocht is de rêst net fynt. Dan komt er wer. Meastal mat er dan hwat ha. De doomny freget him dan wol faek hwer't er forlet fan hat. Dan neamt er dat.\nAs men him dat jowt komt er net wer.\nMar men mat goed oppasse hoe't men it him jowt. Men mat it yn in bûsdoek byelkoar rolje en in tippe fan 'e bûsdoek fêsthâlde. Sa mat men it him jaen. Oars skroeit it fel der ôf. De bûsdoek skroeit nou.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA006903","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At night a minister is surrounded by dark figures, which vanish when he says that if they are of the devil they must go away and if they are of God they must come to him.","place":"Wijckel","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130636","original":"Op in nacht roun to Kipenburch allinne in dûmny op 'e wei. Hy sei: \"Zo alleen op de weg is toch vervelend\". Mar tagelyk seach er ek hwat oankommen. Hy wie by de Skearslipersbrêge, doe't der dûnkere gedaenten om him hinne strúnden. Dûmny sei: \"Als gij van de duivel komt, wijk van mij; komt ge van God, komt tot mij\". Doe wienen de gedaenten samar fordwoun.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111728","role":"member","render":{"description":"When the dead keep wandering after their death, they cannot find rest because they did something wrong or because a promise made to them was not kept. The souls of murdered people also wander at night. A man who treated his wife badly during her life is constantly harassed by her ghost after her death.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29939","original":"Soms dwaelden der minsken op 'e paden om dy't al stoarn wienen. Dy hienen hwat útheefd en koenen de rêst net fine. Of se hienen noch in bigearte, dy't earst yn forfulling gean moest.\nEk guon dy't formoarde wienen dwelmen nachts om. Yn Kollumersweach wie in wiif stoarn, dy har man hie har min bihandele. Nei har dea kaem se hyltyd wer by dy man. Soms roun se njonken him lâns. Hy koe har net wer kwyt wurde.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ002908","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman dies in Egypte and visits her husband every day. The man fetches the minister and the woman tells the minister what she desires. The man does what the woman wants and since then there has been no more haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1950,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/15731","original":"Yn Egypte wenne in man, dy syn wyfke forstoar, mar nei har dea kom se alle dagen by him. Hy helle de dûmny der by, dy't har oanspruts en frege hwat se bigearde. Oan dy dûmny joech se har bigearte to witen. De man foldie oan dy bigearte en it spoekjen wie dien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Wijckel belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2143,"rank":0.7917,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer lives in a haunted farmhouse. When an old soldier comes begging, the farmer asks whether he will keep watch.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35028","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"half","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ015407","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she later goes to feed the pigs, the child's ghost keeps appearing. The child keeps putting its little hands on the pig trough.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ073804","role":"half","render":{"description":"Then Ruerd threatened to knock him down if he did not wait. The other then stopped. When Ruerd reached him, the other grabbed him several times and threw him over the trees. The next day they found him unconscious with all his ribs broken.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight the soldier sees six ghosts pass by; high-ranking officers who dig a hole by the haystack with their sabres. The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093904","role":"half","render":{"description":"He died in an accident with a horse and now his treasure lies there under the ground. The old man haunts the place and people are terrified. The old man keeps coming closer.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ082909","role":"half","render":{"description":"The man cannot bear it and fetches the minister. The minister says to the ghost: 'If you are of God, come to me; if you are of the devil, depart.' The ghost disappears and never comes back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
